nel hasn't yet discussed Candidate C fully. We need to bring C into discussion, perhaps ask for missing info, or evaluate. We need to give a recommendation. We can keep our vote for A, but we need to reference the discussion and maybe ask for more info on C. We need to be concise.\n\nWe have to follow the guidelines: one focused argumentative contribution, referencing prior discussion, using explicit facts, and give a vote.\n\nWe can say: I agree with the shift to A, but we still need to evaluate C's anticipation and leadership versus his interpersonal issues. I propose we ask for any evidence on C's reliability and stress resilience, or we can argue that given the current evidence, A remains best.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: C anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, but is unfriendly, eats unhealthily, show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nWe can argue that C's strengths are valuable but his interpersonal issues are concerning, and we lack evidence on his reliability and stress resilience, so we keep A.\n\nThus our public message: I agree with the shift to A, but we still need to discuss C. I maintain my vote for A.\n\nNow produce the output."}
